-Cancellation requests are not proof of every native executor's termination. Lost acknowledgement
-after committed receipt and cold reconstruction remain separate recovery work; no schema, store,
+Cancellation requests are not proof of every native executor's termination. Stop settlement stages
+persist in existing Session entries, keyed by the original run span and
+branch. Cancellation precedes this fallible persistence. A retry checks accepted receipt identity;
+a cold runner only reconstructs the saved settlement, never restarts the child. An attempted
+notification with unknown acceptance remains explicitly unresolved and cannot be replayed.
+Known pre-admission failures remain retryable. This record is settlement evidence owned by Session,
+not another task or notification queue; no schema, store,
 permission grant, new UI or exactly-once claim is introduced.
+
+Acceptance also covers commit-before-acknowledgement loss with SQLite and a real disposable child,
+cold reconstruction, unknown notification acceptance, and a newer run using the same task ID.
+
+Incomplete cold settlement projects `lost` with an explicit unresolved error, never a live child.
+A derived pending-settlement marker keeps public Stop open even if its last terminal event was
+committed before acknowledgement was lost. Resume writes a pending new-run intent into the same old Stop entry before metadata I/O, then
+admits that exact new run before child execution. Proven rollback restores the original Stop.
+Unknown rollback preserves the original evidence; a persisted pending intent blocks old-artifact
+replay. If admission already committed, the newer run excludes historical Stop reconstruction,
+leaving subsequent child outcome to its existing Session/artifact owners. Branch/run identity is
+rechecked after asynchronous reads and before publication.
+
+Source: ZCode `29628c9` runner retains the original registry/artifact/event/notification owners.
+Pi Core `6fb2e7815167e6b19006fc526d1a5d0f5f998787` `agent.ts:341–351,508–555`
+abort/wait-for-idle is sequencing evidence only; it does not make parent receipts durable.
+Recovery here adapts those existing owners, using Session entries and the background SessionInput
+identity for evidence. SQLite absence cannot prove a synchronous queue callback did not accept work.
+
+Resume setup rechecks the exact new run after each awaited journal/metadata stage before another
+write or execution. Concurrent Stop does not wait to request cancellation behind setup persistence.
+When Stop already owns the run, the stale resume settles SendMessage as interrupted and cannot
+restore the previous registry or artifacts. A terminal pre-ready child explicitly settles the
+readiness caller instead of leaving it waiting forever.
